  "description": "Think you can read the room?\n\nNumbers, formulas, symbols, abbreviations...\nEach clue hides an English word waiting to be discovered.\n\"I think I get it... but what is it again?\"\n\"Oh — that's what it means!\"\nA word puzzle that tests your intuition and English instincts.\n\nIn this game, you'll decode visual clues — numbers, scientific formulas, and symbols — then rearrange the scrambled letters to spell out the hidden English word.\n\nHow to play:\n・Look at the clue and figure out the English word\n・Arrange the scrambled letters in the correct order\n・Reveal the answer — \"So THAT'S what it meant!\"\n\n365 → year / H₂O → water / Au 79 → gold...\nMath, science, computers, music — 100 questions covering all kinds of knowledge.\n\nA fun word puzzle that doubles as English vocabulary practice. Enjoyable for all ages.\nJump in anytime, one question at a time.\n\nCan you read the room?\n\nSupports both button and touch controls. Play in TV mode, tabletop mode, or handheld mode.\n",
